<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#bukhar-khudah">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bukhar Khudah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bukhar Khudah, 'lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a>', was the title of the local rulers of Bukhara before and during the Arab conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a>. The dynasty minted coins and ruled the Zarafshan delta from Varakhsha. It survived as a client of the Arab governors and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samanid-empire">Samanids</a>, and its last members lost their estates in the 9th century.</p></div>
